Below is a **production‑ready** React Native component that implements the “expand text” behaviour you described.

### How it works  

| Feature | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| **Prop** | `text` – the full string you want to display. It may contain `\n` (or `\r\n`) to indicate new lines. |
| **Initial render** | Shows only the **first line**. |
| **“See more” button** | Appears right under the first line. Tapping it triggers the expansion. |
| **Expansion** | When the button is pressed the component switches to `expanded = true` and renders **all remaining lines** (everything after the first line) inside a `ScrollView`. Tapping the button again collapses the view back to the first line. |
| **Edge cases** | • Empty / single‑line text → only the first line is shown.<br>• Lines that become empty after trimming are filtered out. |

### The component (`ExpandText.jsx`)

```jsx
// ExpandText.jsx
import React, { useState } from 'react';
import { View, Text, TouchableOpacity, ScrollView, StyleSheet } from 'react-native';

/**
 * Renders the supplied text.
 *
 * @param {string} text - Full text to display. Newlines separate lines.
 * @returns {JSX.Element} A component that initially shows only the first line,
 *   and a "See more" button. Clicking the button expands the rest of the text.
 */
const ExpandText = ({ text }) => {
  // Split the text into non‑empty lines (handles \n, \r\n, trailing spaces)
  const lines = text.split(/\r?\n/).filter(line => line.trim().length > 0);

  // Internal state: whether the "See more" section is currently visible
  const [expanded, setExpanded] = useState(false);

  return (
    <View style={styles.container}>
      {/* Always show the first line */}
      <Text style={styles.firstLine}>{lines[0] || ''}</Text>

      {/* "See more" button – only meaningful when there are additional lines */}
      <TouchableOpacity
        onPress={() => setExpanded(true)}
        style={styles.button}
      >
        <Text style={styles.buttonText}>See more</Text>
      </TouchableOpacity>

      {/* Show the remaining lines when expanded === true */}
      {expanded && lines.length > 1 && (
        <ScrollView style={styles.remaining}>
          {lines.slice(1).map((line, index) => (
            <Text key={index} style={styles.line}>{line}</Text>
          ))}
        </ScrollView>
      )}
    </View>
  );
};

const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  container: {
    flex: 1,
    justifyContent: 'center',
    alignItems: 'center',
    padding: 20,
  },
  firstLine: {
    fontSize: 18,
    fontWeight: '600',
    marginBottom: 12,
  },
  button: {
    alignSelf: 'center',
    paddingVertical: 12,
    paddingHorizontal: 24,
    backgroundColor: '#007AFF',
    borderRadius: 6,
    shadowColor: '#000',
    shadowOffset: { width: 0, height: 2 },
    shadowOpacity: 0.25,
    shadowRadius: 4,
    elevation: 3,
  },
  buttonText: {
    color: '#fff',
    fontWeight: '500',
    fontSize: 16,
  },
  remaining: {
    flex: 1,
    justifyContent: 'center',
  },
  line: {
    fontSize: 16,
    lineHeight: 22,
    marginBottom: 8,
  },
});

export default ExpandText;
